&gt;[https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/3246303?hl=en](https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/3246303?hl=en)

&nbsp;

From what I can tell, Location Sharing requests aren't exposed via the API (the application programming interface, a set of tools a large tech company provides to developers to allow them to write automation jobs and tools using stuff you can do in the app manually) so that means that whoever wrote the tool generating the message you saw probably found an unpublished end-point and used that to send this message. 

**TLDR SCAM**

