I don't actually like this approach, too many things can be blocked by it, like one of the banking services that we use.  Additionally, I've seen download links blocked by its matching pattern.  For instance, I just ran into an issue where I couldn't download the newest version of a popular multimedia framework because of a network level ad blocker.

&nbsp;

I prefer the ease of an in-browser solution.  IMHO, everyone will eventually encounter an error with a router level ad blocker and they can be very hard to find (mainly because you forget about setting up the filtering!)

The game seems to matchmake solely based on player power...which makes little sense, if you ask me.  Player power level should be ignored for matchmaking. 

What I mean is that the affects of gems or gear skills should be kept, but ignore player CP level.  If this were to happen, then PVP would be more skill based and less grind/pay based, which I think would make for more fun combat.  I'm not sure about you but I \*really\* don't think it's fun to be paired up with someone in Duel PVP who has 1.5 M CP on my character and kills me in three hits.  

